Converter byte-identity — run from the MAIN CHECKOUT, 2026-08-06

Why this file exists
--------------------
verify.sh's converter byte-identity gate is VACUOUS in a worktree. `incoming/`
is gitignored, so `incoming/pricing-templates/` exists only in the main
checkout; `npm run convert:pricing` therefore ENOENTs, writes nothing, and the
gate's `git diff --quiet src/seed/data/price-lists.json` then passes because
nothing ran. verify-20260806T032804Z.log records exactly that:

    ENOENT: no such file or directory, scandir
      '.../w10-pricing-template/atelier-api/incoming/pricing-templates'
        price-lists.json unchanged — exit 0

W10 rewrote the converter, so that gate is the one that mattered. Re-run here
against the real corpus, with the branch's converter and an explicit output
path so neither `incoming/` nor the committed JSON was touched:

    node scripts/convert-price-lists.js \
      /Users/verumoffice/atelier-api/incoming/pricing-templates \
      <scratch>/w10-price-lists.json

Result
------
    Wrote 19514 items from 74 files (40 suppliers, 2 exact duplicate rows dropped)
    cmp <scratch>/w10-price-lists.json src/seed/data/price-lists.json
      -> BYTE IDENTICAL   (8641248 bytes both sides)
    git -C /Users/verumoffice/atelier-api status --porcelain  -> clean
      (incoming/ untouched, committed JSON untouched)

The zero-rate skips reported to stderr (Colefax & Fowler price-on-application
rows, etc.) are the documented behaviour, unchanged.

Gates re-run on the main checkout after the follow-up duty_class fix:
    npm run lint   -> 0
    npm test       -> 0   (40 files, 749 tests)
    npm run migrate -> 0, twice, second run "No migrations to run!"
